.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_MAC-CMAC 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_MAC-CMAC
.Nd The CMAC EVP_MAC implementation
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Support for computing CMAC MACs through the
.Sy EVP_MAC
API.
.Pp
This implementation uses EVP_CIPHER functions to get access to the
underlying cipher.
.Ss Identity
This implementation is identified with this name and properties, to be
used with
.Xr EVP_MAC_fetch 3 :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqCMAC", \(dqprovider=default" or \(dqprovider=fips"
.El
.Ss Supported parameters
The general description of these parameters can be found in
.Xr EVP_MAC 3 .
.Pp
The following parameter can be set with
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_set_params 3 :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqkey" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_KEY Ns ) <octet string>
Sets the MAC key.
Setting this parameter is identical to passing a
.Em key
to
.Xr EVP_MAC_init 3 .
.It \(dqcipher" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_CIPHER Ns ) <UTF8 string>
Sets the name of the underlying cipher to be used.
The mode of the cipher must be CBC.
.It \(dqproperties" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_PROPERTIES Ns ) <UTF8 string>
Sets the properties to be queried when trying to fetch the underlying
cipher.
This must be given together with the cipher naming parameter to be
considered valid.
.It \(dqencrypt-check" ( Ns Sy OSSL_CIPHER_PARAM_FIPS_ENCRYPT_CHECK Ns ) <integer>
This option is used by the OpenSSL FIPS provider.
If required this parameter should be set before
.Xr EVP_MAC_init 3
.Pp
The default value of 1 causes an error when a unapproved Triple-DES
encryption operation is triggered.
Setting this to 0 will ignore the error and set the approved
"fips-indicator" to 0. This option breaks FIPS compliance if it causes
the approved "fips-indicator" to return 0.
.El
.Pp
The following parameters can be retrieved with
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_get_params 3 :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqsize" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_SIZE Ns ) <unsigned integer>
The "size" parameter can also be retrieved with with
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_get_mac_size 3 .
The length of the "size" parameter is equal to that of an
.Sy unsigned int .
.It \(dqblock-size" ( Ns Sy OSSL_MAC_PARAM_BLOCK_SIZE Ns ) <unsigned integer>
Gets the MAC block size.
The "block-size" parameter can also be retrieved with
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_get_block_size 3 .
.It \(dqfips-indicator" ( Ns Sy OSSL_CIPHER_PARAM_FIPS_APPROVED_INDICATOR Ns ) <integer>
This option is used by the OpenSSL FIPS provider.
.Pp
A getter that returns 1 if the operation is FIPS approved, or 0
otherwise.
This may be used after calling
.Xr EVP_MAC_final 3 .
It may return 0 if the "encrypt-check" option is set to 0.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_get_params 3 ,
.Xr EVP_MAC_CTX_set_params 3 ,
.Xr EVP_MAC 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
